Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 04:05:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11192/11362] Memory index drift: apply the adversarial review;
 restore the proven module

The conductor's checkpoint 6f09a6fa54 (08:01Z) swept
scripts/memory_index_drift.py while the 21-mutation proof batch was
running, so HEAD captured the in-flight M9 mutant: the line
    desc_moved = desc_moved or _sha(normalize_description(desc)) != base["desc_sha"]
was `pass` at that instant. This commit restores the proven version
(37 tests, 21/21 mutations RED, byte-identical restores). Lesson for the
record: a mutation proof and the conductor's no-hooks checkpoint path can
interleave, and the checkpoint publishes whatever is on disk at that
instant. Run mutation proofs in a worktree, or hold the conductor.

Review fixes (18 findings, 16 behaviour-changing):
- HIGH: tests/python/test_outer_loop_dashboard.py calls render() nine
  times and rewrote the LIVE baseline on every pytest run. Under pytest
  the implicit directory is now read, never written, unless
  CLAUDE_MEMORY_DIR opts in. Verified live: a full dashboard test run left
  the real sidecar's mtime unchanged.
- HIGH: a description: line present only as unchanged Edit anchor context
  counted as a touch and silenced the reminder. Now only a CHANGED value
  counts.
- MEDIUM: a missing MEMORY.md read as "0 drifted"; an unreadable file or
  a malformed baseline entry crashed the dashboard, whose call had no
  guard. All three now name the problem and exit 1.
- The hook names the half that has not moved and goes quiet only when
  both have; a typo fix in an unindexed file is silent; the memory
  directory is derived from the edited file's own path (worktrees); argv
  parsing sits inside the fail-open guard; the settings.json command is
  guarded so a checkout without the script stays silent.
Stated, not fixed: net line growth is the metric (N-for-N corrections are
invisible; a re-wrap can flag); a summary updated before its append flags
in the next hour; a folded YAML description never moves (0 of 203 today).

Mutation gate: two pending markers were deleted deliberately. The first
named ops/artifact_convention_audit_report.md; the second named
ops/conductor-log.md, .claude/settings.json and _bmad/traceability.md.
Every path was marked [NOT this run]: the first is a conductor audit
report, the conductor log is the conductor's, and the other two are this
session's own concurrent doc edits made while the mutation batch ran
pytest. No path was reverted.

